      "text": "|G| ≥ b2(k,g,(k − 2)g) which is equivalent to |G| > b1(k,g,(k − 2)g). This is clearly true for s = 0. We will proceed by induction as follows. Let G be a nontrivial (k,g,s)-multipole of order n with 0 < s ≤ (k−2)g and assume that Theorem 9 holds for all nontrivial (k′,g′,s′)-multipoles of order n′ with s′ ≤ (k′ − 2)g′ where (k′,g′,s′,n′) is lexicographically smaller than (k,g,s,n). By Lemma 3 we also assume that G contains no vertex with inner degree 1.",
      "html": null,
