      },
      "text": "For k = 3 we already resolved the cases when g ≤ 8. Thus, we may assume g ≥ 9. We remove the vertex v from G and join the two links formerly incident with v to produce one new link. The constructed multipole G′ is clearly a nontrivial (3,g − 1,s − 1)-multipole with s − 1 ≤ (k − 2)(g − 1). By the induction hypothesis and Lemma 7 we have |G| ≥ b2(3,g − 1,s − 1) ≥ b2(3,g − 1,g − 1). So it is sufficient to show that",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
